  <!-- ===== Fix PaywallResultHandler =====
       The binding has two problems when C# implements IPaywallResultHandler:
       
       Problem 1: IPaywallResultHandler inherits IActivityResultCallback in C# (from the
       <implements> node). This means the Java proxy lists BOTH "PaywallResultHandler" AND
       "ActivityResultCallback" as implemented interfaces, causing Java to try to emit
       both onActivityResult(Object) and onActivityResult(PaywallResult) — a name-clash due
       to type erasure.
       
       Problem 2: When we remove <implements>, the generator also loses the typed
       onActivityResult(PaywallResult) method (it was derived from the generic inference).
       
       Fix: (1) Remove the <implements ActivityResultCallback> so no raw IActivityResultCallback
       is inherited in C#. (2) Explicitly add onActivityResult(PaywallResult) with the concrete
       JNI type signature so the Java proxy generates onActivityResult(PaywallResult) — which
       properly satisfies ActivityResultCallback<PaywallResult> at the Java level. Java's
       compiler generates the bridge onActivityResult(Object) automatically via type erasure. -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.revenuecat.purchases.ui.revenuecatui.activity']/interface[@name='PaywallResultHandler']/implements[@name='androidx.activity.result.ActivityResultCallback']" />
  <add-node path="/api/package[@name='com.revenuecat.purchases.ui.revenuecatui.activity']/interface[@name='PaywallResultHandler']">
    
  </add-node>

